  "meta": {
    "bibkey": "engelhardt-etal-2006",
    "method": "experiment",
    "description": "Three experiments on the Gricean maxim of Quantity with displays of an apple on a towel, an empty towel, an empty box and either a frog or a second apple. In Experiment 1 speakers instruct a confederate to move the apple, and the first instruction of each trial is coded for a modified target; in Experiments 2 and 2b listeners rate instructions from 1 (incorrect) to 5 (perfect), Experiment 2b replacing *put the apple on the towel* by *put the apple on the other towel*; Experiment 3 records eye movements, not tabled here. Tests are printed by subjects (F1), by items (F2) and as min F'; their degrees of freedom are in the notes. Pairwise comparisons of condition means are read against the 95% confidence interval of their difference. The speech files were offered at a lab address that no longer resolves; no data were released.",
